  "body": "Found by the independent review of PR #346 (2026-11-08 ~23:40 local): `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` run from `crates/ui` on plain `origin/main` fails 2 tests, both pixel diffs:\n\n- `egui_shell_snapshot_light`\n- `tool_editor_snapshot`\n\nThey fail identically on main without #346, so one of today's merges changed the light shell / tool editor render without regenerating its goldens (candidates merged since the last green UI run: #324 ribbon Setups cell + browser row, #328/#331 work-offset labels and Setups/Heights rows, #341 part-alignment row, #346 plane row, #188 status strip). The dark `egui_shell_snapshot` was not reported failing - check it too.\n\n**Done means:** find the merge that changed the render (bisect with the two tests), confirm the visual change is intended (inspect the `.new.png` against the golden), regenerate the goldens with `UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1` from `crates/ui`, and the full ui lib is green on main again. If the diff is NOT an intended change, fix the regression instead.\n\nRelated: #255 (move pixel goldens out of the PR flow) - this is the cost it describes.\n",
